{"tool_name":"trycycler","contents":["biocontainers","galaxy","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"trycycler","version":"0.5.6","home":"https://github.com/rrwick/Trycycler","documentation":"https://github.com/rrwick/Trycycler/wiki","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"Trycycler is a tool for generating consensus long-read assemblies for bacterial genomes.","identifiers":["doi:10.1186/s13059-021-02483-z","biotools:trycycler","usegalaxy-eu:trycycler_cluster","usegalaxy-eu:trycycler_consensus","usegalaxy-eu:trycycler_partition","usegalaxy-eu:trycycler_reconcile_msa","usegalaxy-eu:trycycler_subsample"],"license_file":"LICENSE","build":{"entry_points":["trycycler = trycycler.__main__:main"],"noarch":"python","number":0,"run_exports":[null],"script":"-m pip install --no-deps --no-build-isolation --no-cache-dir --use-pep517 . -vvv"},"requirements":{"host":["python >=3.9","pip","setuptools"],"run":["python >=3.9","python-edlib","setuptools","scipy","numpy","pillow","miniasm","minimap2","mash","muscle <4","r-base","r-ape","r-phangorn"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/rrwick/Trycycler/archive/v0.5.6.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["trycycler --version","trycycler subsample --help","trycycler cluster --help","trycycler dotplot --help","trycycler reconcile --help","trycycler msa --help","trycycler partition --help","trycycler consensus --help"]},"recipe_maintainers":["thanhleviet","galladoalba"]},"biocontainers":{"name":"trycycler","identifiers":["doi:10.5281/zenodo.3965017"],"license":"Not available","summary":"Trycycler is a tool for generating consensus long-read assemblies for bacterial genomes","home_url":"https://github.com/rrwick/Trycycler","keywords":[],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":859},"biotools":{"id":"trycycler","home":"http://github.com/rrwick/Trycycler-paper","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Trycycler: consensus long-read assemblies for bacterial genomes","addition_date":"2021-11-15T17:51:21.603316Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-07T10:09:04.108022Z","tool_type":["Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:trycycler","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Jane Hawkey"},{"name":"Louise M. Judd"},{"name":"Louise T. Cerdeira"},{"name":"Ryan R. Wick","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8349-0778"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["rlibouban"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0525"},{"term":"Scaffold gap completion","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3217"},{"term":"Sequence assembly validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3180"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"}]}],"name":"Trycycler","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-021-02483-z","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).While long-read sequencing allows for the complete assembly of bacterial genomes, long-read assemblies contain a variety of errors. Here, we present Trycycler, a tool which produces a consensus assembly from multiple input assemblies of the same genome. Benchmarking showed that Trycycler assemblies contained fewer errors than assemblies constructed with a single tool. Post-assembly polishing further reduced errors and Trycycler+polishing assemblies were the most accurate genomes in our study. As Trycycler requires manual intervention, its output is not deterministic. However, we demonstrated that multiple users converge on similar assemblies that are consistently more accurate than those produced by automated assembly tools.","authors":[{"name":"Cerdeira L.T."},{"name":"Hawkey J."},{"name":"Holt K.E."},{"name":"Judd L.M."},{"name":"Meric G."},{"name":"Vezina B."},{"name":"Wick R.R."},{"name":"Wyres K.L."}],"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"Trycycler: consensus long-read assemblies for bacterial genomes"},"pmcid":"PMC8442456","pmid":"34521459"}],